From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 05:40:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] winspool: a printer's location and description follow CUPS (9214)

A CUPS printer's location and description were copied when the printer was
first added and never again: changed in CUPS (lpadmin -L/-D, Settings, the
Print to PDF queue's new location), Windows programs went on showing the old
words (the Print dialog's Where:). When the printers are made again from
CUPS's (its printers.conf changed), an existing printer now takes CUPS's
current location and description.
Gate test/cupsjobs-gate.sh location part; mutant SG_MUTANT_STALE_LOCATION.
---
--- a/dlls/winspool.drv/info.c
+++ b/dlls/winspool.drv/info.c
@@ -888,6 +888,13 @@
 
             TRACE("Printer already exists\n");
             RegDeleteValueW( printer_key, May_Delete_Value );
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_STALE_LOCATION
+            /* Stained Glass OS (9214): what CUPS says of the queue now -- its
+             * location and description -- not what it said when the printer
+             * was added (a location changed with lpadmin -L stayed the old one) */
+            if (printer->location) set_reg_szW( printer_key, L"Location", printer->location );
+            if (printer->comment) set_reg_szW( printer_key, L"Description", printer->comment );
+#endif
             driver = cups_queue_driver( model, printer_key, &windows );
             if (windows)
             {
